  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscPat2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'Your care team explains that patients may be invited to share their
    perspectives early in the research process so researchers can understand what
    matters most in daily life and design studies that reflect those needs.

    <b>By
    including patient voices early, new treatments are more likely to be safer and
    more effective for more people.</b>

    Is this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: When patients, particularly those from historically underrepresented
    groups, share their experiences, researchers can design studies that better reflect
    real-world needs. While it is not guaranteed that every new treatment will ever
    work for every patient, diverse patient perspectives increase the chances that
    discoveries will lead to safer, more effective treatments that benefit as many
    people as possible.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
